    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Paul was founded in the scenic Loup River Valley, a spot that drew early settlers to its fertile lands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://stpaulnebraska.com/community/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors the Paul brothers, the surveyors who laid out the original that’ll become St. Paul.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early St. Paul boasted a diverse industrial mix, from broom and canning factories to brickworks, cigar shops, flour mills, and a hatchery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During its first twenty years, Howard County, where St. Paul sits, was a typical western frontier filled with covered wagons, cowboys, and railroad construction gangs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "St. Paul officially became Howard County’s seat in 1874 and was incorporated as a city in 1881.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Hall of Fame pitcher Grover Cleveland Alexander was born on a farm near St. Paul and later retired to the town.",
